From 9b9c73f163f053ddd45c14526d7c03bb9de01ccd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: barracuda156 <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 01:33:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 50/60] ppc32: no lock-free two-word freelist head on 32-bit
 PowerPC

First G5 cycle of the 13.6 port, parade #1 (every TU that reaches
wasm-code-pointer-table.h: enum-verifiers.cc, class-verifiers.cc,
exported-macros-assembler.cc, ... fail the same way):

  src/common/segmented-table.h:124:44: error: static assertion failed
    static_assert(std::atomic<FreelistHead>::is_always_lock_free);
  'std::atomic<SegmentedTable<WasmCodePointerTableEntry,
   134217728>::FreelistHead>::is_always_lock_free' evaluates to false

13.6 generalised the sandbox tables' segmented freelist into
SegmentedTable and made the wasm code-pointer table an unconditional
instance of it (12.4 only had the ExternalEntityTable version, under
V8_COMPRESS_POINTERS and so never compiled here).  FreelistHead is two
uint32s; upstream's 32-bit hosts (arm with ldrexd/strexd, ia32 with
cmpxchg8b) make an 8-byte atomic lock-free, 32-bit PowerPC does not:
lwarx/stwcx. are word-sized (the 970 can do ldarx/stdcx. in 32-bit
mode, but the baseline is generic ppc), so gcc routes 8-byte atomics
to libatomic's locked implementation and is_always_lock_free is
false.  Drop the assert on that host: the freelist_head_ load/store/
compare_exchange in wasm-code-pointer-table-inl.h compile unchanged
against libatomic (-latomic is already on the link line and already
carries the SharedArrayBuffer i64 atomics that 0036 routes through
the C++ runtime), the mutual exclusion is just a lock instead of a
reservation.
---
 v8/src/common/segmented-table.h | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/v8/src/common/segmented-table.h b/v8/src/common/segmented-table.h
index 41b5983..94bd4c3 100644
--- a/v8/src/common/segmented-table.h
+++ b/v8/src/common/segmented-table.h
@@ -121,7 +121,14 @@ class V8_EXPORT_PRIVATE SegmentedTable {
 
   // We expect the FreelistHead struct to fit into a single atomic word.
   // Otherwise, access to it would be slow.
+#if V8_HOST_ARCH_PPC && V8_HOST_ARCH_32_BIT
+  // 32-bit PowerPC has no 64-bit reservation pair (lwarx/stwcx. are
+  // word-sized), so the two-word head goes through libatomic's locked
+  // fallback instead: slower, not wrong.  The same path already carries
+  // the SharedArrayBuffer i64 atomics on this target.
+#else
   static_assert(std::atomic<FreelistHead>::is_always_lock_free);
+#endif
 
   SegmentedTable() = default;
   SegmentedTable(const SegmentedTable&) = delete;
-- 
